  <h1>Frame Multiplier — Request setup</h1>
  <p class="updated">Setup is free. You pay only if you release the frames.</p>

  <p>Send us your Figma file and we set up the masters and run the rollout for you. You see every
    size as a low-res JPEG preview before you decide anything.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Share the file.</strong> In Figma, click Share, set the link to
      <strong>Anyone with the link · can view</strong>, and paste it below. View access is enough:
      we work on our own copy, so nobody is added to your team and your file is not edited.</li>
    <li><strong>We check the artwork.</strong> If it doesn't suit a rollout we reply and say why,
      and that is the end of it.</li>
    <li><strong>We send previews.</strong> You get a view-only link to our copy, with every size
      filled by a low-res JPEG of its layout.</li>
    <li><strong>You release the frames.</strong> Releasing costs $1 a frame, with a $99 minimum
      per rollout. On payment we replace the JPEGs with the working frames and hand the file over.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What to have ready</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Your finished master layouts on one page of the file.</li>
    <li>The list of sizes you need, in the file or in the note below.</li>
    <li>The names of the fonts used. If one is not a Google or Adobe font, say so and we will ask
      how to get it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your request</h2>

  <form class="req-form" id="req-form" action="https://formspree.io/f/xljbayey" method="POST">
    <label for="req-name">Your name</label>
    <input type="text" id="req-name" name="name" autocomplete="name" required>

    <label for="req-email">Email</label>
    <input type="email" id="req-email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required>

    <label for="req-link">Figma file link
      <span class="hint">Set to "Anyone with the link · can view".</span></label>
    <input type="url" id="req-link" name="figma_link" placeholder="https://www.figma.com/design/…" required>

    <label for="req-note">Sizes and notes
      <span class="hint">The sizes you need, the fonts used, and anything we should know about the artwork.</span></label>
    <textarea id="req-note" name="notes"></textarea>

    <input type="hidden" name="plugin_release" id="req-v" value="">
    <input type="hidden" name="plugin_summary" id="req-s" value="">
    <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Frame Multiplier setup request">
    <input type="text" name="_gotcha" class="req-trap" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" aria-hidden="true">

    <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" id="req-send">Send request</button>
  </form>

  <div class="callout req-result" id="req-ok" role="status">
    <p><strong>Request sent.</strong> We reply by email once we have looked at the file.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="callout req-result" id="req-fail" role="alert">
    <p><strong>The request did not send.</strong> Check your connection and try again, or email the
      same details to <a href="mailto:{% endraw %}{{ site.support }}{% raw %}">{% endraw %}{{ site.support }}{% raw %}</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="req-note">This form is sent through Formspree. It carries what you type above and, when
    you arrive from the plugin, the plugin's release number and the line shown in its summary bar.
    No part of your design is sent by the plugin or by this form.</p>

  <p class="req-note">To do the work we copy your file into our own Figma account. We keep that copy
    for 30 days after the file is handed back to you, then delete it.</p>

  <script>
    (function () {
      var q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      document.getElementById('req-v').value = (q.get('v') || '').slice(0, 40);
      document.getElementById('req-s').value = (q.get('s') || '').slice(0, 200);
      var form = document.getElementById('req-form');
      var send = document.getElementById('req-send');
      var show = function (id) {
        document.getElementById('req-ok').classList.toggle('is-shown', id === 'req-ok');
        document.getElementById('req-fail').classList.toggle('is-shown', id === 'req-fail');
      };
      // Without script the form still posts and Formspree shows its own confirmation page.
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (ev) {
        if (!window.fetch) return;
        ev.preventDefault();
        send.disabled = true;
        fetch(form.action, { method: 'POST', body: new FormData(form), headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } })
          .then(function (r) {
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error('refused');
            form.hidden = true;
            show('req-ok');
          })
          .catch(function () { send.disabled = false; show('req-fail'); });
      });
    })();
  </script>
{% endraw %}
